        "market_heading": "Why home staging matters in the Seattle market",
        "market_text": "<p>Seattle and the Eastside run on tech relocation. Buyers arriving for roles in Bellevue, Redmond and South Lake Union are often house-hunting from another city, sometimes another country, on a start-date deadline. The listing photos are the entire tour until the week they land.</p><p>The light is a genuine technical problem here for much of the year. An empty white-walled condo photographed under overcast Puget Sound skies has almost no warmth in it, and no amount of exposure correction adds the furniture, texture and colour that make a room feel lived in. Home staging is what puts that back.</p><p>Bellevue and downtown Seattle also skew heavily to towers, where a one-bedroom unit photographs like every other one-bedroom in the building. When the floor plan is shared by forty other listings, the staging is the only thing distinguishing yours in the scroll.</p>",
